    {
      "id": "rigi_mavs_ifnb",
      "title": "RIG-I/MAVS → IFN-β",
      "pathway": "Cytosolic RNA Sensing → IRF3 → IFN-β",
      "renderer": "builtin",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "roundsToUnlock": 3,
      "slotsPerRound": 2,
      "description": "Cytosolic viral RNA — including short double-stranded RNA and 5'-triphosphate single-stranded RNA — is sensed by the helicase RIG-I (encoded by DDX58). Binding exposes RIG-I's CARD domains, which signal through MAVS (Mitochondrial Antiviral Signaling protein) anchored on the mitochondrial outer membrane.",
      "teachingPoint": "MAVS forms prion-like filaments on the mitochondria that amplify signaling to the TBK1 kinase. TBK1 phosphorylates IRF3 at multiple C-terminal serine residues, causing IRF3 homodimerization and nuclear translocation to drive IFN-β transcription. This axis is essential for innate defense against RNA viruses including influenza, Sendai virus, and SARS-CoV-2.",
